window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b219-2c5bd3f5ea32d2ce.json"]={sha256:"2c5bd3f5ea32d2ce6ae1a10bc4eaadf73db566579a7e9e1737c5106c7010fa9b",value:{"id":"b219","title":"曾文水庫大壩","titleEn":"Tsengwen Dam","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"曾文案例將土石壩內的有效應力及排水，連到下游串聯水庫、灌溉渠道與水能利用。學生把閘門出流、消能功率與泥砂質量分開記帳，再核對渠道容量、田間需水及壩頂沉陷趨勢。全課以假想資料檢驗物理關係，避免把容量相加當成可以任意調度的同一水池。","summaryEn":"The Tsengwen case links effective stress and drainage inside an embankment to downstream serial storage, irrigation canals and energy recovery. Learners keep gate discharge, dissipated power and sediment mass in separate accounts before checking canal capacity, field demand and settlement trends. Hypothetical data test physical relationships without treating two reservoir capacities as one freely interchangeable pool.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-dams","subcategoryTitle":"世界水壩與水庫","subcategoryTitleEn":"World dams and reservoirs","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-dams","learningTags":["water","water-dams","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["串聯水庫的內部轉水","Internal transfers in serial reservoirs"],["排水層的導水阻力","Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer"],["消能區的功率通量","Power flux in a dissipating reach"],["共同放流的發電與灌溉","Energy and irrigation from one release"],["田間淨需水與毛取水","Net field need and gross withdrawal"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["串聯水庫的內部轉水","排水層的導水阻力","消能區的功率通量","共同放流的發電與灌溉","田間淨需水與毛取水"],"labelsEn":["Internal transfers in serial reservoirs","Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer","Power flux in a dissipating reach","Energy and irrigation from one release","Net field need and gross withdrawal"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"假想曾文上游水池每天流入一百二十萬立方公尺，輸往下游八十萬、其他損失十萬，蓄量增加三十萬立方公尺。下游接收八十萬，灌溉取走七十萬、損失五萬，增加五萬；全系統增加三十五萬，內部轉水應互相抵銷。若下游需求增百分之二十到八十四萬，下游轉成減少九萬而全系統只增二十一萬。另以六百毫米淨灌溉水深、兩百公頃及效率零點七五求得毛需水一百六十萬立方公尺，不可把效率損失重複扣算。 核驗：Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day。先各寫一份水量表，再把上游轉出與下游收到配對相消；若旅行時間跨日，需在輸水段另列暫存。以兩池水位庫容變化獨立核對，避免只因合計帳平衡就忽略某一池資料錯誤。","textEn":"Assume the upper reservoir receives 1.2 million m3 per day, transfers 0.8 million and loses 0.1 million; storage rises by 0.3 million m3. The lower pool receives that transfer, supplies 0.7 million and loses 0.05 million, gaining 0.05 million. System storage therefore rises by 0.35 million, with the internal transfer cancelling. Raising lower demand twenty percent to 0.84 million makes its change negative 0.09 million and the system gain 0.21 million. Separately, a 600 mm net depth over 200 ha at efficiency 0.75 requires 1.6 million m3 gross supply. Verification: Write separate balances and cancel matched upper exports and lower receipts. If travel crosses the daily boundary, include storage in the conveyance segment. Independently compare both pool level-volume changes so a balanced total does not conceal an error in one reservoir.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b219-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「串聯水庫的內部轉水」與「壩體孔壓與有效應力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs\" and \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b219-v15-01","title":"串聯水庫的內部轉水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「串聯水庫的內部轉水」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Internal transfers in serial reservoirs” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"曾文與烏山頭的串聯背景提醒水量帳必須選好邊界：對上游水庫而言轉送是流出，對下游是流入，但對合併系統而言它只是內部交換。分池蓄量仍很重要，因為下游需求不能無視輸水能力與旅行時間。兩池總量增加不代表每池都增加，更不表示水可以立即任意調往任何位置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「串聯水庫的內部轉水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Serial storage requires explicit boundaries: a transfer leaves the upper reservoir and enters the lower one, but cancels within the combined system. Individual storage still matters because downstream demand is constrained by conveyance capacity and travel time. A rise in combined storage does not imply that both pools rise, nor that water can move instantly and freely to any location where demand occurs. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Internal transfers in serial reservoirs” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day.","failure":"常見誤解：「上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「串聯水庫的內部轉水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Internal transfers in serial reservoirs”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-01-k1","title":"串聯水庫的內部轉水","titleEn":"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs","text":"曾文與烏山頭的串聯背景提醒水量帳必須選好邊界：對上游水庫而言轉送是流出，對下游是流入，但對合併系統而言它只是內部交換。分池蓄量仍很重要，因為下游需求不能無視輸水能力與旅行時間。","textEn":"Serial storage requires explicit boundaries: a transfer leaves the upper reservoir and enters the lower one, but cancels within the combined system. Individual storage still matters because downstream demand is constrained by conveyance capacity and travel time.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「串聯水庫的內部轉水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs\" is correct?","options":["上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源","曾文與烏山頭的串聯背景提醒水量帳必須選好邊界：對上游水庫而言轉送是流出，對下游是流入，但對合併系統而言它只是內部交換。","孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力"],"optionsEn":["Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources","Serial storage requires explicit boundaries: a transfer leaves the upper reservoir and enters the lower one, but cancels within the combined system.","Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton"],"answer":1,"explanation":"曾文與烏山頭的串聯背景提醒水量帳必須選好邊界：對上游水庫而言轉送是流出，對下游是流入，但對合併系統而言它只是內部交換。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Serial storage requires explicit boundaries: a transfer leaves the upper reservoir and enters the lower one, but cancels within the combined system. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b219-v15-02","title":"串聯水庫的內部轉水：定量估算","titleEn":"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「串聯水庫的內部轉水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Internal transfers in serial reservoirs” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day。適用邊界：同一日封閉雙池系統，內部轉水抵銷，沒有額外下游天然入流。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day. Applicable boundary: A two-pool daily system with internal transfers cancelling and no additional natural inflow to the lower pool. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先各寫一份水量表，再把上游轉出與下游收到配對相消；若旅行時間跨日，需在輸水段另列暫存。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Write separate balances and cancel matched upper exports and lower receipts.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day。適用邊界：同一日封閉雙池系統，內部轉水抵銷，沒有額外下游天然入流。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day. Applicable boundary: A two-pool daily system with internal transfers cancelling and no additional natural inflow to the lower pool.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「串聯水庫的內部轉水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs\", which statement holds?","options":["不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式","原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多","原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day。"],"optionsEn":["The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level","Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval","Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Vin=1200000 m3/day."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Vin=1200000 m3/day; demand=700000 m3/day; lossUpper=100000 m3/day; lossLower=50000 m3/day; dVsystem=Vin-demand-lossUpper-lossLower=350000 m3/day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b219-v15-03","title":"串聯水庫的內部轉水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「串聯水庫的內部轉水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Internal transfers in serial reservoirs” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先各寫一份水量表，再把上游轉出與下游收到配對相消；若旅行時間跨日，需在輸水段另列暫存。以兩池水位庫容變化獨立核對，避免只因合計帳平衡就忽略某一池資料錯誤。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Write separate balances and cancel matched upper exports and lower receipts. If travel crosses the daily boundary, include storage in the conveyance segment. Independently compare both pool level-volume changes so a balanced total does not conceal an error in one reservoir. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將下游需求增加百分之二十，重新求系統與各池蓄量差，再指定內部轉水八十萬立方公尺每天，證明總帳不因轉水名稱而改變。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase downstream demand twenty percent and calculate system and individual changes using a transfer of eight hundred thousand cubic metres per day. Show that relabeling internal transfer cannot alter the combined balance.","failure":"注意干擾：把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先各寫一份水量表，再把上游轉出與下游收到配對相消；若旅行時間跨日，需在輸水段另列暫存。以兩池水位庫容變化獨立核對，避免只因合計帳平衡就忽略某一池資料錯誤。","textEn":"Write separate balances and cancel matched upper exports and lower receipts. If travel crosses the daily boundary, include storage in the conveyance segment. Independently compare both pool level-volume changes so a balanced total does not conceal an error in one reservoir.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將下游需求增加百分之二十，重新求系統與各池蓄量差，再指定內部轉水八十萬立方公尺每天，證明總帳不因轉水名稱而改變。","textEn":"Increase downstream demand twenty percent and calculate system and individual changes using a transfer of eight hundred thousand cubic metres per day. Show that relabeling internal transfer cannot alter the combined balance.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「串聯水庫的內部轉水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs\"?","options":["先各寫一份水量表，再把上游轉出與下游收到配對相消；若旅行時間跨日，需在輸水段另列暫存。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深"],"optionsEn":["Write separate balances and cancel matched upper exports and lower receipts.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先各寫一份水量表，再把上游轉出與下游收到配對相消；若旅行時間跨日，需在輸水段另列暫存。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Write separate balances and cancel matched upper exports and lower receipts. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b219-v15-04","title":"串聯水庫的內部轉水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「串聯水庫的內部轉水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Internal transfers in serial reservoirs” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources. Checking only combined storage can hide a lower-pool shortage while water remains upstream but cannot be conveyed quickly enough to meet demand. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：兩池總量增加不代表每池都增加，更不表示水可以立即任意調往任何位置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A rise in combined storage does not imply that both pools rise, nor that water can move instantly and freely to any location where demand occurs.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。","textEn":"Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources. Checking only combined storage can hide a lower-pool shortage while water remains upstream but cannot be conveyed quickly enough to meet demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「串聯水庫的內部轉水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。","孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources.","Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b219-v15-05","title":"壩體孔壓與有效應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「壩體孔壓與有效應力」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"土石壩顆粒骨架承擔有效應力，水的孔隙壓力則分擔總法向應力。以總應力減孔壓可說明排水與蓄水變化如何影響骨架受力，但這是單點應力關係，不直接等於整體抗滑能力。若土未飽和或有明顯各向異性，還需要更適當的有效應力描述與材料參數，不能把飽和模型無條件外推。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壩體孔壓與有效應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The soil skeleton carries effective stress while pore water contributes to total normal stress. Subtracting pore pressure illustrates how drainage and reservoir changes affect skeleton loading, but this point relation does not establish whole-slope resistance. Unsaturated conditions or pronounced anisotropy require additional constitutive description and material parameters, so the saturated model cannot be extended indiscriminately to every location or stage of embankment response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壩體孔壓與有效應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-05-k1","title":"壩體孔壓與有效應力","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress","text":"土石壩顆粒骨架承擔有效應力，水的孔隙壓力則分擔總法向應力。以總應力減孔壓可說明排水與蓄水變化如何影響骨架受力，但這是單點應力關係，不直接等於整體抗滑能力。","textEn":"The soil skeleton carries effective stress while pore water contributes to total normal stress. Subtracting pore pressure illustrates how drainage and reservoir changes affect skeleton loading, but this point relation does not establish whole-slope resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壩體孔壓與有效應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\" is correct?","options":["孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力","總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞","土石壩顆粒骨架承擔有效應力，水的孔隙壓力則分擔總法向應力。"],"optionsEn":["Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton","Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked","The soil skeleton carries effective stress while pore water contributes to total normal stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"土石壩顆粒骨架承擔有效應力，水的孔隙壓力則分擔總法向應力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The soil skeleton carries effective stress while pore water contributes to total normal stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b219-v15-06","title":"壩體孔壓與有效應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壩體孔壓與有效應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa。適用邊界：飽和土單一法向分量，壓應力為正，未計剪應力或安全係數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa. Applicable boundary: One normal component in saturated soil with compression positive, excluding shear stress and a safety factor. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對土壓計與測壓管是否代表同一位置、方向與時段，再比較水位升降時兩者變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm that earth-pressure and pore-pressure measurements represent matching location, direction and time, then compare their changes during level cycles.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa。適用邊界：飽和土單一法向分量，壓應力為正，未計剪應力或安全係數。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa. Applicable boundary: One normal component in saturated soil with compression positive, excluding shear stress and a safety factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壩體孔壓與有效應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa。","每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力","發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa.","Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure","Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b219-v15-07","title":"壩體孔壓與有效應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壩體孔壓與有效應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對土壓計與測壓管是否代表同一位置、方向與時段，再比較水位升降時兩者變化。將量測高程與水壓基準寫清楚，並以多點剖面辨識局部孔壓，避免把一個平均值套到整個壩坡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm that earth-pressure and pore-pressure measurements represent matching location, direction and time, then compare their changes during level cycles. Record elevation and pressure datum and use multiple points to identify local conditions rather than assigning one average to an entire slope. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：固定總應力，把孔壓提高五十千帕後重算，再畫總應力、孔壓與有效應力三條示意線，說明若總應力也變動時為何不能只看水壓。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hold total stress fixed and raise pore pressure fifty kilopascals, then sketch total, pore and effective stress. Explain why pressure alone is insufficient when total stress changes at the same time.","failure":"注意干擾：把孔壓當作額外壓緊土粒的力而相加，會把有效應力方向算反；排水堵塞時總應力可能近似不變而骨架有效應力下降，僅看總壓力會漏掉變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adding pore pressure as extra particle clamping reverses the effective-stress relation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對土壓計與測壓管是否代表同一位置、方向與時段，再比較水位升降時兩者變化。將量測高程與水壓基準寫清楚，並以多點剖面辨識局部孔壓，避免把一個平均值套到整個壩坡。","textEn":"Confirm that earth-pressure and pore-pressure measurements represent matching location, direction and time, then compare their changes during level cycles. Record elevation and pressure datum and use multiple points to identify local conditions rather than assigning one average to an entire slope.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"固定總應力，把孔壓提高五十千帕後重算，再畫總應力、孔壓與有效應力三條示意線，說明若總應力也變動時為何不能只看水壓。","textEn":"Hold total stress fixed and raise pore pressure fifty kilopascals, then sketch total, pore and effective stress. Explain why pressure alone is insufficient when total stress changes at the same time.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壩體孔壓與有效應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對土壓計與測壓管是否代表同一位置、方向與時段，再比較水位升降時兩者變化。","兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Confirm that earth-pressure and pore-pressure measurements represent matching location, direction and time, then compare their changes during level cycles.","An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely"],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對土壓計與測壓管是否代表同一位置、方向與時段，再比較水位升降時兩者變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm that earth-pressure and pore-pressure measurements represent matching location, direction and time, then compare their changes during level cycles. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b219-v15-08","title":"壩體孔壓與有效應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壩體孔壓與有效應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把孔壓當作額外壓緊土粒的力而相加，會把有效應力方向算反；排水堵塞時總應力可能近似不變而骨架有效應力下降，僅看總壓力會漏掉變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adding pore pressure as extra particle clamping reverses the effective-stress relation. During drainage blockage, total stress may stay almost unchanged while skeleton stress falls, so total-pressure observations alone can miss the important change. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若土未飽和或有明顯各向異性，還需要更適當的有效應力描述與材料參數，不能把飽和模型無條件外推。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Unsaturated conditions or pronounced anisotropy require additional constitutive description and material parameters, so the saturated model cannot be extended indiscriminately to every location or stage of embankment response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把孔壓當作額外壓緊土粒的力而相加，會把有效應力方向算反；排水堵塞時總應力可能近似不變而骨架有效應力下降，僅看總壓力會漏掉變化。","textEn":"Adding pore pressure as extra particle clamping reverses the effective-stress relation. During drainage blockage, total stress may stay almost unchanged while skeleton stress falls, so total-pressure observations alone can miss the important change.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壩體孔壓與有效應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞","把孔壓當作額外壓緊土粒的力而相加，會把有效應力方向算反；排水堵塞時總應力可能近似不變而骨架有效應力下降，僅看總壓力會漏掉變化。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked","Adding pore pressure as extra particle clamping reverses the effective-stress relation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把孔壓當作額外壓緊土粒的力而相加，會把有效應力方向算反；排水堵塞時總應力可能近似不變而骨架有效應力下降，僅看總壓力會漏掉變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adding pore pressure as extra particle clamping reverses the effective-stress relation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b219-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「排水層的導水阻力」與「假想閘下出流量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer\" and \"Hypothetical gated underflow\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b219-v15-09","title":"排水層的導水阻力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「排水層的導水阻力」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"下游排水層提供較低阻力通路，讓穿過心層的水離開並降低孔壓。達西式可由流量反推所需水頭損失，顯示濾料堵塞或有效面積縮小會提高上游水頭。導水良好與保土功能是兩個要求，材料粗化雖能降低阻力，卻不一定維持對細料的截留，不能只追求最大流量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水層的導水阻力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A downstream drain offers a lower-resistance path for seepage and helps limit pore pressure. Rearranging Darcy's relation gives the head loss required to pass a flow, showing why clogging or reduced effective area increases upstream head. Hydraulic capacity and soil retention are separate requirements: coarser material may reduce resistance without retaining fines, so maximizing flow alone does not define a satisfactory filter-drain system. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排水層的導水阻力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-09-k1","title":"排水層的導水阻力","titleEn":"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer","text":"下游排水層提供較低阻力通路，讓穿過心層的水離開並降低孔壓。達西式可由流量反推所需水頭損失，顯示濾料堵塞或有效面積縮小會提高上游水頭。","textEn":"A downstream drain offers a lower-resistance path for seepage and helps limit pore pressure. Rearranging Darcy's relation gives the head loss required to pass a flow, showing why clogging or reduced effective area increases upstream head.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排水層的導水阻力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer\" is correct?","options":["下游排水層提供較低阻力通路，讓穿過心層的水離開並降低孔壓。","總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞","不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式"],"optionsEn":["A downstream drain offers a lower-resistance path for seepage and helps limit pore pressure.","Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked","The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level"],"answer":0,"explanation":"下游排水層提供較低阻力通路，讓穿過心層的水離開並降低孔壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A downstream drain offers a lower-resistance path for seepage and helps limit pore pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b219-v15-10","title":"排水層的導水阻力：定量估算","titleEn":"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排水層的導水阻力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m。適用邊界：均勻飽和達西流、固定有效截面，不代表現地排水層能力驗收。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m. Applicable boundary: Uniform saturated Darcy flow through fixed effective area, not a field drain-capacity acceptance test. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以排水層前後的測壓差與總排水量反算導水能力，確認出口未被回水淹沒。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Infer conductance from head difference and total drainage while checking for outlet submergence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m。適用邊界：均勻飽和達西流、固定有效截面，不代表現地排水層能力驗收。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m. Applicable boundary: Uniform saturated Darcy flow through fixed effective area, not a field drain-capacity acceptance test.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排水層的導水阻力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer\", which statement holds?","options":["原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多","原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m。","矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深"],"optionsEn":["Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval","Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m.","Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=0.006 m3/s; L=12 m; k=0.003 m/s; A=24 m2; dh=Q L/(k A)=1 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b219-v15-11","title":"排水層的導水阻力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水層的導水阻力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以排水層前後的測壓差與總排水量反算導水能力，確認出口未被回水淹沒。將維護清理、細料出現與降雨時段一起標記，再檢查水頭升高是來水增加還是阻力增加，不能只看流量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Infer conductance from head difference and total drainage while checking for outlet submergence. Mark cleaning, observed fines and rainfall periods, then determine whether rising head reflects increased inflow or increased resistance rather than interpreting discharge alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把滲透係數減半並保持流量不變，重算所需水頭差，再把截面也減少四分之一，比較兩種劣化疊加的效果與量測所需證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve permeability at fixed flow and recalculate required head difference, then also reduce area by one quarter. Compare the combined effects and identify measurements needed to distinguish the two deterioration mechanisms.","failure":"注意干擾：出口回水會改變水頭邊界，若仍把出口當零壓就錯估阻力；局部堵塞也可能讓水改走旁路，使總排水量近似不變卻在壩內形成不同孔壓分布。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Outlet backwater changes the hydraulic boundary, so assuming zero outlet pressure misestimates resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以排水層前後的測壓差與總排水量反算導水能力，確認出口未被回水淹沒。將維護清理、細料出現與降雨時段一起標記，再檢查水頭升高是來水增加還是阻力增加，不能只看流量。","textEn":"Infer conductance from head difference and total drainage while checking for outlet submergence. Mark cleaning, observed fines and rainfall periods, then determine whether rising head reflects increased inflow or increased resistance rather than interpreting discharge alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把滲透係數減半並保持流量不變，重算所需水頭差，再把截面也減少四分之一，比較兩種劣化疊加的效果與量測所需證據。","textEn":"Halve permeability at fixed flow and recalculate required head difference, then also reduce area by one quarter. Compare the combined effects and identify measurements needed to distinguish the two deterioration mechanisms.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排水層的導水阻力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率","以排水層前後的測壓差與總排水量反算導水能力，確認出口未被回水淹沒。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency","Infer conductance from head difference and total drainage while checking for outlet submergence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以排水層前後的測壓差與總排水量反算導水能力，確認出口未被回水淹沒。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Infer conductance from head difference and total drainage while checking for outlet submergence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b219-v15-12","title":"排水層的導水阻力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排水層的導水阻力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出口回水會改變水頭邊界，若仍把出口當零壓就錯估阻力；局部堵塞也可能讓水改走旁路，使總排水量近似不變卻在壩內形成不同孔壓分布。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Outlet backwater changes the hydraulic boundary, so assuming zero outlet pressure misestimates resistance. Local blockage can redirect flow through bypasses, leaving total drainage similar while changing the internal pore-pressure distribution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：導水良好與保土功能是兩個要求，材料粗化雖能降低阻力，卻不一定維持對細料的截留，不能只追求最大流量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hydraulic capacity and soil retention are separate requirements: coarser material may reduce resistance without retaining fines, so maximizing flow alone does not define a satisfactory filter-drain system.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出口回水會改變水頭邊界，若仍把出口當零壓就錯估阻力；局部堵塞也可能讓水改走旁路，使總排水量近似不變卻在壩內形成不同孔壓分布。","textEn":"Outlet backwater changes the hydraulic boundary, so assuming zero outlet pressure misestimates resistance. Local blockage can redirect flow through bypasses, leaving total drainage similar while changing the internal pore-pressure distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排水層的導水阻力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hydraulic resistance of a drain layer\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["出口回水會改變水頭邊界，若仍把出口當零壓就錯估阻力；局部堵塞也可能讓水改走旁路，使總排水量近似不變卻在壩內形成不同孔壓分布。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式"],"optionsEn":["Outlet backwater changes the hydraulic boundary, so assuming zero outlet pressure misestimates resistance.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level"],"answer":0,"explanation":"出口回水會改變水頭邊界，若仍把出口當零壓就錯估阻力；局部堵塞也可能讓水改走旁路，使總排水量近似不變卻在壩內形成不同孔壓分布。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Outlet backwater changes the hydraulic boundary, so assuming zero outlet pressure misestimates resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b219-v15-13","title":"假想閘下出流量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hypothetical gated underflow: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「假想閘下出流量」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hypothetical gated underflow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"閘下出流把上游水頭轉成高速水流，開口面積與局部收縮共同控制通量。用孔口形式可作量級比較，但真實閘門出流還要分自由與淹沒狀態，並知道上游能量與尾水。曾文案例的教學參數完全是假想，不是現地閘門開度表，計算目的是理解水頭平方根與開口面積的一次關係。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「假想閘下出流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gated underflow converts upstream head into high-speed flow, with opening area and contraction controlling discharge. An orifice-style relation supports scale comparison, but actual gates require distinction between free and submerged conditions and knowledge of upstream energy and tailwater. All parameters here are hypothetical rather than a Tsengwen gate schedule; the purpose is to distinguish square-root head dependence from linear dependence on opening area. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hypothetical gated underflow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「假想閘下出流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hypothetical gated underflow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-13-k1","title":"假想閘下出流量","titleEn":"Hypothetical gated underflow","text":"閘下出流把上游水頭轉成高速水流，開口面積與局部收縮共同控制通量。用孔口形式可作量級比較，但真實閘門出流還要分自由與淹沒狀態，並知道上游能量與尾水。","textEn":"Gated underflow converts upstream head into high-speed flow, with opening area and contraction controlling discharge. An orifice-style relation supports scale comparison, but actual gates require distinction between free and submerged conditions and knowledge of upstream energy and tailwater.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「假想閘下出流量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hypothetical gated underflow\" is correct?","options":["不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式","閘下出流把上游水頭轉成高速水流，開口面積與局部收縮共同控制通量。","每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力"],"optionsEn":["The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level","Gated underflow converts upstream head into high-speed flow, with opening area and contraction controlling discharge.","Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"閘下出流把上游水頭轉成高速水流，開口面積與局部收縮共同控制通量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gated underflow converts upstream head into high-speed flow, with opening area and contraction controlling discharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b219-v15-14","title":"假想閘下出流量：定量估算","titleEn":"Hypothetical gated underflow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「假想閘下出流量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hypothetical gated underflow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s。適用邊界：假想矩形自由出流開口，水頭以開口中心計，未計尾水淹沒。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s. Applicable boundary: A hypothetical rectangular free-discharge opening with head measured to its center and no tailwater submergence. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫出開口中心與自由水面，核對水頭定義後用量水設施求實際係數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw opening center and free surface, verify the head definition and infer discharge coefficient from measurements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s。適用邊界：假想矩形自由出流開口，水頭以開口中心計，未計尾水淹沒。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s. Applicable boundary: A hypothetical rectangular free-discharge opening with head measured to its center and no tailwater submergence.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「假想閘下出流量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hypothetical gated underflow\", which statement holds?","options":["發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗","兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推","原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s。"],"optionsEn":["Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water","An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely","Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Cd=0.65."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b219-v15-15","title":"假想閘下出流量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hypothetical gated underflow: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「假想閘下出流量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hypothetical gated underflow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫出開口中心與自由水面，核對水頭定義後用量水設施求實際係數。比較不同開度的係數是否穩定，記錄尾水變化和水面波動，再決定簡單孔口式是否足以描述該測試區間。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw opening center and free surface, verify the head definition and infer discharge coefficient from measurements. Compare coefficients across openings while recording tailwater and surface fluctuations before deciding whether a simple orifice relation describes the tested range. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將假想開口高度減半但暫維持中心水頭，求流量變化，再重新加入中心位置改變，說明分步比較有助於分辨面積與水頭兩種效應。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve opening height while temporarily holding center head fixed, then account for the changed center elevation. Explain how the two-step comparison separates area effects from the effect of altered hydraulic head.","failure":"注意干擾：把開口高度改變造成的中心高程變化完全忽略，會使大幅開度比較不一致；尾水淹沒後仍使用自由出流式，則可能高估通量並錯配下游水量帳。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring the changing opening-center elevation can make comparisons inconsistent over large opening changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫出開口中心與自由水面，核對水頭定義後用量水設施求實際係數。比較不同開度的係數是否穩定，記錄尾水變化和水面波動，再決定簡單孔口式是否足以描述該測試區間。","textEn":"Draw opening center and free surface, verify the head definition and infer discharge coefficient from measurements. Compare coefficients across openings while recording tailwater and surface fluctuations before deciding whether a simple orifice relation describes the tested range.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將假想開口高度減半但暫維持中心水頭，求流量變化，再重新加入中心位置改變，說明分步比較有助於分辨面積與水頭兩種效應。","textEn":"Halve opening height while temporarily holding center head fixed, then account for the changed center elevation. Explain how the two-step comparison separates area effects from the effect of altered hydraulic head.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「假想閘下出流量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hypothetical gated underflow\"?","options":["畫出開口中心與自由水面，核對水頭定義後用量水設施求實際係數。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源"],"optionsEn":["Draw opening center and free surface, verify the head definition and infer discharge coefficient from measurements.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources"],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫出開口中心與自由水面，核對水頭定義後用量水設施求實際係數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw opening center and free surface, verify the head definition and infer discharge coefficient from measurements. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b219-v15-16","title":"假想閘下出流量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hypothetical gated underflow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「假想閘下出流量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hypothetical gated underflow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把開口高度改變造成的中心高程變化完全忽略，會使大幅開度比較不一致；尾水淹沒後仍使用自由出流式，則可能高估通量並錯配下游水量帳。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring the changing opening-center elevation can make comparisons inconsistent over large opening changes. Retaining a free-discharge equation after submergence can overstate flow and distort the downstream water balance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：曾文案例的教學參數完全是假想，不是現地閘門開度表，計算目的是理解水頭平方根與開口面積的一次關係。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: All parameters here are hypothetical rather than a Tsengwen gate schedule; the purpose is to distinguish square-root head dependence from linear dependence on opening area.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把開口高度改變造成的中心高程變化完全忽略，會使大幅開度比較不一致；尾水淹沒後仍使用自由出流式，則可能高估通量並錯配下游水量帳。","textEn":"Ignoring the changing opening-center elevation can make comparisons inconsistent over large opening changes. Retaining a free-discharge equation after submergence can overstate flow and distort the downstream water balance.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「假想閘下出流量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hypothetical gated underflow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把開口高度改變造成的中心高程變化完全忽略，會使大幅開度比較不一致；尾水淹沒後仍使用自由出流式，則可能高估通量並錯配下游水量帳。","每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Ignoring the changing opening-center elevation can make comparisons inconsistent over large opening changes.","Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把開口高度改變造成的中心高程變化完全忽略，會使大幅開度比較不一致；尾水淹沒後仍使用自由出流式，則可能高估通量並錯配下游水量帳。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring the changing opening-center elevation can make comparisons inconsistent over large opening changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b219-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「消能區的功率通量」與「近底取水的輸砂效率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Power flux in a dissipating reach\" and \"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b219-v15-17","title":"消能區的功率通量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Power flux in a dissipating reach: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「消能區的功率通量」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Power flux in a dissipating reach” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"溢流水失去的水頭代表機械能轉為紊流、熱與聲等形式，流量乘水頭損失可求耗散功率。把功率除以示意面積得到平均面功率通量，有助比較能量集中程度，但單位不是壓力，不能直接當作混凝土或岩盤承受的力。局部沖刷還取決於流向、脈動、材料與持續時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「消能區的功率通量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Head lost by spill flow represents mechanical energy converted to turbulence, heat and sound. Discharge times head loss gives dissipated power, and dividing by an illustrative area gives mean areal power flux. This compares energy concentration but is not pressure or a structural force. Local scour additionally depends on flow direction, fluctuations, material resistance and duration, so equal mean flux does not imply equal damage. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Power flux in a dissipating reach” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「消能區的功率通量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Power flux in a dissipating reach”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-17-k1","title":"消能區的功率通量","titleEn":"Power flux in a dissipating reach","text":"溢流水失去的水頭代表機械能轉為紊流、熱與聲等形式，流量乘水頭損失可求耗散功率。把功率除以示意面積得到平均面功率通量，有助比較能量集中程度，但單位不是壓力，不能直接當作混凝土或岩盤承受的力。","textEn":"Head lost by spill flow represents mechanical energy converted to turbulence, heat and sound. Discharge times head loss gives dissipated power, and dividing by an illustrative area gives mean areal power flux.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「消能區的功率通量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Power flux in a dissipating reach\" is correct?","options":["每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力","原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多","溢流水失去的水頭代表機械能轉為紊流、熱與聲等形式，流量乘水頭損失可求耗散功率。"],"optionsEn":["Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure","Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval","Head lost by spill flow represents mechanical energy converted to turbulence, heat and sound."],"answer":2,"explanation":"溢流水失去的水頭代表機械能轉為紊流、熱與聲等形式，流量乘水頭損失可求耗散功率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Head lost by spill flow represents mechanical energy converted to turbulence, heat and sound. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b219-v15-18","title":"消能區的功率通量：定量估算","titleEn":"Power flux in a dissipating reach: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「消能區的功率通量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Power flux in a dissipating reach” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2。適用邊界：耗散能量在假想面積上的平均分配，不是局部衝擊壓力或沖刷深度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2. Applicable boundary: Mean dissipated power over a hypothetical area, not local impact pressure or scour depth. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先以總功率核對流量與水頭損失，再確認除以面積後單位仍含每秒能量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check total power from flow and head loss, then retain the energy-per-time unit after division by area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2。適用邊界：耗散能量在假想面積上的平均分配，不是局部衝擊壓力或沖刷深度。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2. Applicable boundary: Mean dissipated power over a hypothetical area, not local impact pressure or scour depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「消能區的功率通量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Power flux in a dissipating reach\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2。","矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深","毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3.","Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth","Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=35 m3/s; dH=18 m; A=140 m2; flux=rho g Q dH/A/1000=44.145 kW/m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b219-v15-19","title":"消能區的功率通量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Power flux in a dissipating reach: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「消能區的功率通量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Power flux in a dissipating reach” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先以總功率核對流量與水頭損失，再確認除以面積後單位仍含每秒能量。比較水槽中的流態與壓力脈動量測，將面功率圖與沖刷地形分開呈現，避免以同一色階暗示兩者一一對應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check total power from flow and head loss, then retain the energy-per-time unit after division by area. Compare flume flow patterns and pressure fluctuations, presenting power-flux and scour maps separately rather than suggesting a one-to-one relationship through shared coloring. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把分配面積加倍求平均通量變化，再畫一半功率集中在十分之一面積的情境，計算局部通量並說明平均值何時可能掩蓋集中作用。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double the assumed distribution area and recalculate mean flux, then concentrate half the power in one tenth of the area. Calculate local flux and explain how a mean can hide concentration.","failure":"注意干擾：把千瓦每平方公尺誤寫成千帕會混淆能量速率與受力；平均分散範圍即使很大，局部射流仍可能集中撞擊，因此均值低不能排除局部侵蝕熱點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Relabeling kilowatts per square metre as kilopascals confuses energy rate with force. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先以總功率核對流量與水頭損失，再確認除以面積後單位仍含每秒能量。比較水槽中的流態與壓力脈動量測，將面功率圖與沖刷地形分開呈現，避免以同一色階暗示兩者一一對應。","textEn":"Check total power from flow and head loss, then retain the energy-per-time unit after division by area. Compare flume flow patterns and pressure fluctuations, presenting power-flux and scour maps separately rather than suggesting a one-to-one relationship through shared coloring.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把分配面積加倍求平均通量變化，再畫一半功率集中在十分之一面積的情境，計算局部通量並說明平均值何時可能掩蓋集中作用。","textEn":"Double the assumed distribution area and recalculate mean flux, then concentrate half the power in one tenth of the area. Calculate local flux and explain how a mean can hide concentration.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「消能區的功率通量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Power flux in a dissipating reach\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","先以總功率核對流量與水頭損失，再確認除以面積後單位仍含每秒能量。","孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check total power from flow and head loss, then retain the energy-per-time unit after division by area.","Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton"],"answer":1,"explanation":"先以總功率核對流量與水頭損失，再確認除以面積後單位仍含每秒能量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check total power from flow and head loss, then retain the energy-per-time unit after division by area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b219-v15-20","title":"消能區的功率通量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Power flux in a dissipating reach: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「消能區的功率通量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Power flux in a dissipating reach” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把千瓦每平方公尺誤寫成千帕會混淆能量速率與受力；平均分散範圍即使很大，局部射流仍可能集中撞擊，因此均值低不能排除局部侵蝕熱點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Relabeling kilowatts per square metre as kilopascals confuses energy rate with force. Even a broad mean dissipation area may contain a concentrated jet, so low average flux cannot exclude a local erosion hotspot. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：局部沖刷還取決於流向、脈動、材料與持續時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Local scour additionally depends on flow direction, fluctuations, material resistance and duration, so equal mean flux does not imply equal damage.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把千瓦每平方公尺誤寫成千帕會混淆能量速率與受力；平均分散範圍即使很大，局部射流仍可能集中撞擊，因此均值低不能排除局部侵蝕熱點。","textEn":"Relabeling kilowatts per square metre as kilopascals confuses energy rate with force. Even a broad mean dissipation area may contain a concentrated jet, so low average flux cannot exclude a local erosion hotspot.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「消能區的功率通量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Power flux in a dissipating reach\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多","把千瓦每平方公尺誤寫成千帕會混淆能量速率與受力；平均分散範圍即使很大，局部射流仍可能集中撞擊，因此均值低不能排除局部侵蝕熱點。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval","Relabeling kilowatts per square metre as kilopascals confuses energy rate with force."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把千瓦每平方公尺誤寫成千帕會混淆能量速率與受力；平均分散範圍即使很大，局部射流仍可能集中撞擊，因此均值低不能排除局部侵蝕熱點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Relabeling kilowatts per square metre as kilopascals confuses energy rate with force. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b219-v15-21","title":"近底取水的輸砂效率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「近底取水的輸砂效率」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"靠近底部的取水可能攜帶較濃泥砂，但輸砂效果應用乾固體質量與放流水量共同衡量，而非只說水看起來很濁。質量濃度本身就是每單位水混合物體積攜帶的固體，乘流量才變成質量率。沉積物是否能被帶到入口，還取決於地形與流場，計算輸出不等於證明整個庫底被清除。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「近底取水的輸砂效率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Withdrawal near the bottom may carry more concentrated sediment, but performance requires both dry-solids mass and released water volume rather than visual darkness. Concentration measures solids per mixture volume, and multiplication by flow gives mass rate. Whether deposits reach the inlet depends on bed geometry and flow, so a calculated export does not demonstrate clearance of the entire reservoir floor or uniform sediment removal. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne.","failure":"常見誤解：「原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「近底取水的輸砂效率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-21-k1","title":"近底取水的輸砂效率","titleEn":"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal","text":"靠近底部的取水可能攜帶較濃泥砂，但輸砂效果應用乾固體質量與放流水量共同衡量，而非只說水看起來很濁。質量濃度本身就是每單位水混合物體積攜帶的固體，乘流量才變成質量率。","textEn":"Withdrawal near the bottom may carry more concentrated sediment, but performance requires both dry-solids mass and released water volume rather than visual darkness. Concentration measures solids per mixture volume, and multiplication by flow gives mass rate.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「近底取水的輸砂效率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal\" is correct?","options":["靠近底部的取水可能攜帶較濃泥砂，但輸砂效果應用乾固體質量與放流水量共同衡量，而非只說水看起來很濁。","原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多","發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗"],"optionsEn":["Withdrawal near the bottom may carry more concentrated sediment, but performance requires both dry-solids mass and released water volume rather than visual darkness.","Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval","Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"靠近底部的取水可能攜帶較濃泥砂，但輸砂效果應用乾固體質量與放流水量共同衡量，而非只說水看起來很濁。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Withdrawal near the bottom may carry more concentrated sediment, but performance requires both dry-solids mass and released water volume rather than visual darkness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b219-v15-22","title":"近底取水的輸砂效率：定量估算","titleEn":"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「近底取水的輸砂效率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne。適用邊界：一小時均勻假想懸浮濃度，非曾文實際設備排砂率或操作條件。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne. Applicable boundary: One hour of uniform hypothetical suspended concentration, not actual Tsengwen equipment performance or operation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將代表水樣乾燥後求固體濃度，核對採樣口是否避開粗粒沉降而偏低。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Dry representative samples to determine solids concentration and check whether sampler placement misses settling coarse grains.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne。適用邊界：一小時均勻假想懸浮濃度，非曾文實際設備排砂率或操作條件。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne. Applicable boundary: One hour of uniform hypothetical suspended concentration, not actual Tsengwen equipment performance or operation.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「近底取水的輸砂效率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推","原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne。","上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源"],"optionsEn":["An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely","Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne.","Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b219-v15-23","title":"近底取水的輸砂效率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「近底取水的輸砂效率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將代表水樣乾燥後求固體濃度，核對採樣口是否避開粗粒沉降而偏低。同步積分放流水量，再以取水前後庫底測量檢查材料來源，區分新入流通過與既有沉積再搬運。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Dry representative samples to determine solids concentration and check whether sampler placement misses settling coarse grains. Integrate released water simultaneously and compare bed surveys to distinguish passage of new incoming sediment from remobilization of previously deposited material. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設另一時段流量加倍但濃度降為三分之一，計算等長時段的輸出質量和用水量，分別比較總輸砂與每單位水的輸砂，不混為同一效率。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double flow while reducing concentration to one third for an equal duration. Compare total solids, water volume and solids per unit water, keeping those performance measures distinct rather than combining them into one undefined efficiency.","failure":"注意干擾：只以高濃度宣稱效率高可能忽略放流水量很小，總輸出仍有限；反之大量低濃度放流可能耗水多而帶走固體少，兩者需要同一質量與水量邊界才可比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High concentration alone may accompany little water and limited total export. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將代表水樣乾燥後求固體濃度，核對採樣口是否避開粗粒沉降而偏低。同步積分放流水量，再以取水前後庫底測量檢查材料來源，區分新入流通過與既有沉積再搬運。","textEn":"Dry representative samples to determine solids concentration and check whether sampler placement misses settling coarse grains. Integrate released water simultaneously and compare bed surveys to distinguish passage of new incoming sediment from remobilization of previously deposited material.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設另一時段流量加倍但濃度降為三分之一，計算等長時段的輸出質量和用水量，分別比較總輸砂與每單位水的輸砂，不混為同一效率。","textEn":"Double flow while reducing concentration to one third for an equal duration. Compare total solids, water volume and solids per unit water, keeping those performance measures distinct rather than combining them into one undefined efficiency.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「近底取水的輸砂效率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞","將代表水樣乾燥後求固體濃度，核對採樣口是否避開粗粒沉降而偏低。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked","Dry representative samples to determine solids concentration and check whether sampler placement misses settling coarse grains."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將代表水樣乾燥後求固體濃度，核對採樣口是否避開粗粒沉降而偏低。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Dry representative samples to determine solids concentration and check whether sampler placement misses settling coarse grains. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b219-v15-24","title":"近底取水的輸砂效率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「近底取水的輸砂效率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以高濃度宣稱效率高可能忽略放流水量很小，總輸出仍有限；反之大量低濃度放流可能耗水多而帶走固體少，兩者需要同一質量與水量邊界才可比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High concentration alone may accompany little water and limited total export. A large dilute release may consume much water while carrying few solids; both cases require consistent mass and water boundaries for comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：沉積物是否能被帶到入口，還取決於地形與流場，計算輸出不等於證明整個庫底被清除。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Whether deposits reach the inlet depends on bed geometry and flow, so a calculated export does not demonstrate clearance of the entire reservoir floor or uniform sediment removal.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以高濃度宣稱效率高可能忽略放流水量很小，總輸出仍有限；反之大量低濃度放流可能耗水多而帶走固體少，兩者需要同一質量與水量邊界才可比較。","textEn":"High concentration alone may accompany little water and limited total export. A large dilute release may consume much water while carrying few solids; both cases require consistent mass and water boundaries for comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「近底取水的輸砂效率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只以高濃度宣稱效率高可能忽略放流水量很小，總輸出仍有限；反之大量低濃度放流可能耗水多而帶走固體少，兩者需要同一質量與水量邊界才可比較。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗"],"optionsEn":["High concentration alone may accompany little water and limited total export.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只以高濃度宣稱效率高可能忽略放流水量很小，總輸出仍有限；反之大量低濃度放流可能耗水多而帶走固體少，兩者需要同一質量與水量邊界才可比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High concentration alone may accompany little water and limited total export. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b219-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「共同放流的發電與灌溉」與「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Energy and irrigation from one release\" and \"Manning scale for an irrigation canal\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b219-v15-25","title":"共同放流的發電與灌溉：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Energy and irrigation from one release: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「共同放流的發電與灌溉」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Energy and irrigation from one release” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同一股水可以先經發電再用於灌溉，利用位能不等於把水體消耗掉，因此能源與水量可提供不同服務。帳目應把通過機組的水列為同一次放流，避免再加成第二份供水；實際是否可共用仍受渠道高程、時間和取水位置限制。發電效率影響能量轉換，不直接把相同比例水量變成不可用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「共同放流的發電與灌溉」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"One release may generate electricity before serving irrigation; extracting potential energy does not consume the water itself. The turbine flow therefore remains a single water transfer rather than a second supply allocation. Actual reuse depends on canal elevation, timing and withdrawal location. Conversion efficiency changes electrical output, not the fraction of water physically remaining, so energy and water ledgers must use different units and boundaries. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Energy and irrigation from one release” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW.","failure":"常見誤解：「發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「共同放流的發電與灌溉」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Energy and irrigation from one release”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-25-k1","title":"共同放流的發電與灌溉","titleEn":"Energy and irrigation from one release","text":"同一股水可以先經發電再用於灌溉，利用位能不等於把水體消耗掉，因此能源與水量可提供不同服務。帳目應把通過機組的水列為同一次放流，避免再加成第二份供水；實際是否可共用仍受渠道高程、時間和取水位置限制。","textEn":"One release may generate electricity before serving irrigation; extracting potential energy does not consume the water itself. The turbine flow therefore remains a single water transfer rather than a second supply allocation.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共同放流的發電與灌溉」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Energy and irrigation from one release\" is correct?","options":["發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗","同一股水可以先經發電再用於灌溉，利用位能不等於把水體消耗掉，因此能源與水量可提供不同服務。","矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深"],"optionsEn":["Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water","One release may generate electricity before serving irrigation; extracting potential energy does not consume the water itself.","Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同一股水可以先經發電再用於灌溉，利用位能不等於把水體消耗掉，因此能源與水量可提供不同服務。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"One release may generate electricity before serving irrigation; extracting potential energy does not consume the water itself. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b219-v15-26","title":"共同放流的發電與灌溉：定量估算","titleEn":"Energy and irrigation from one release: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「共同放流的發電與灌溉」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Energy and irrigation from one release” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW。適用邊界：同一放流先經假想機組再到下游，未計渠道損失或真實取水配置。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW. Applicable boundary: One release passes a hypothetical unit before downstream use, excluding canal losses and actual withdrawal configuration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在流程圖上用一條水線連接發電與灌溉，另畫能量輸出箭頭，核對單位不混用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw one water path through generation to irrigation with a separate energy-output arrow, checking units.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW。適用邊界：同一放流先經假想機組再到下游，未計渠道損失或真實取水配置。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW. Applicable boundary: One release passes a hypothetical unit before downstream use, excluding canal losses and actual withdrawal configuration.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共同放流的發電與灌溉」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Energy and irrigation from one release\", which statement holds?","options":["毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率","孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力","原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW。"],"optionsEn":["Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency","Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton","Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=8 m3/s; H=60 m; eta=0.86; P=rho g Q H eta/1e6=4.049568 MW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b219-v15-27","title":"共同放流的發電與灌溉：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Energy and irrigation from one release: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「共同放流的發電與灌溉」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Energy and irrigation from one release” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在流程圖上用一條水線連接發電與灌溉，另畫能量輸出箭頭，核對單位不混用。比較機組出口及渠道入口累積流量，將中間損失或暫存另外列帳，確認沒有因兩種用途而重複計水。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw one water path through generation to irrigation with a separate energy-output arrow, checking units. Compare cumulative turbine-outlet and canal-inlet flows, accounting for intermediate losses or storage so two services do not create duplicate water allocations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用同一流量求一日通過水量，再計一日發電量，將兩者以各自單位並列。若渠道另損失百分之五，只修改下游水量帳並說明是否改變已發出的電。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate daily water throughput and energy at the same flow, displaying their distinct units. Apply a separate five-percent canal loss only to downstream water and explain whether it changes electricity already generated.","failure":"注意干擾：把機組效率低於一解讀成同樣比例水被消耗，會錯估下游可用水；把發電用水與灌溉用水相加成總需求，又可能對同一串聯放流重複扣帳。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Interpreting efficiency below unity as an equal loss of water misstates downstream availability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在流程圖上用一條水線連接發電與灌溉，另畫能量輸出箭頭，核對單位不混用。比較機組出口及渠道入口累積流量，將中間損失或暫存另外列帳，確認沒有因兩種用途而重複計水。","textEn":"Draw one water path through generation to irrigation with a separate energy-output arrow, checking units. Compare cumulative turbine-outlet and canal-inlet flows, accounting for intermediate losses or storage so two services do not create duplicate water allocations.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用同一流量求一日通過水量，再計一日發電量，將兩者以各自單位並列。若渠道另損失百分之五，只修改下游水量帳並說明是否改變已發出的電。","textEn":"Calculate daily water throughput and energy at the same flow, displaying their distinct units. Apply a separate five-percent canal loss only to downstream water and explain whether it changes electricity already generated.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共同放流的發電與灌溉」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Energy and irrigation from one release\"?","options":["在流程圖上用一條水線連接發電與灌溉，另畫能量輸出箭頭，核對單位不混用。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式"],"optionsEn":["Draw one water path through generation to irrigation with a separate energy-output arrow, checking units.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在流程圖上用一條水線連接發電與灌溉，另畫能量輸出箭頭，核對單位不混用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw one water path through generation to irrigation with a separate energy-output arrow, checking units. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b219-v15-28","title":"共同放流的發電與灌溉：失效診斷","titleEn":"Energy and irrigation from one release: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「共同放流的發電與灌溉」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Energy and irrigation from one release” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把機組效率低於一解讀成同樣比例水被消耗，會錯估下游可用水；把發電用水與灌溉用水相加成總需求，又可能對同一串聯放流重複扣帳。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Interpreting efficiency below unity as an equal loss of water misstates downstream availability. Adding generation and irrigation water as separate demands can likewise subtract the same serial release twice. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：發電效率影響能量轉換，不直接把相同比例水量變成不可用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Conversion efficiency changes electrical output, not the fraction of water physically remaining, so energy and water ledgers must use different units and boundaries.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把機組效率低於一解讀成同樣比例水被消耗，會錯估下游可用水；把發電用水與灌溉用水相加成總需求，又可能對同一串聯放流重複扣帳。","textEn":"Interpreting efficiency below unity as an equal loss of water misstates downstream availability. Adding generation and irrigation water as separate demands can likewise subtract the same serial release twice.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共同放流的發電與灌溉」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Energy and irrigation from one release\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把機組效率低於一解讀成同樣比例水被消耗，會錯估下游可用水；把發電用水與灌溉用水相加成總需求，又可能對同一串聯放流重複扣帳。","矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Interpreting efficiency below unity as an equal loss of water misstates downstream availability.","Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把機組效率低於一解讀成同樣比例水被消耗，會錯估下游可用水；把發電用水與灌溉用水相加成總需求，又可能對同一串聯放流重複扣帳。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Interpreting efficiency below unity as an equal loss of water misstates downstream availability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b219-v15-29","title":"灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Manning scale for an irrigation canal: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Manning scale for an irrigation canal” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"開放渠道的平均流速受斷面形狀、濕周、坡度及粗糙阻力共同控制。矩形斷面水力半徑是面積除濕周，不等於水深，尤其窄渠道差異顯著。曼寧式可估算均勻流通水量，但回水、閘門控制或急變流會破壞水面坡與底坡近似相同的條件，需要另作水面線分析。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mean open-channel velocity depends on geometry, wetted perimeter, slope and roughness. For a rectangular section, hydraulic radius is area divided by wetted perimeter, not simply depth, especially in a narrow canal. Manning's relation estimates uniform-flow capacity, while backwater, gates or rapidly varied flow can invalidate the approximation that energy slope follows bed slope and require a water-surface-profile calculation instead. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Manning scale for an irrigation canal” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Manning scale for an irrigation canal”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-29-k1","title":"灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度","titleEn":"Manning scale for an irrigation canal","text":"開放渠道的平均流速受斷面形狀、濕周、坡度及粗糙阻力共同控制。矩形斷面水力半徑是面積除濕周，不等於水深，尤其窄渠道差異顯著。","textEn":"Mean open-channel velocity depends on geometry, wetted perimeter, slope and roughness. For a rectangular section, hydraulic radius is area divided by wetted perimeter, not simply depth, especially in a narrow canal.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Manning scale for an irrigation canal\" is correct?","options":["矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深","兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推","開放渠道的平均流速受斷面形狀、濕周、坡度及粗糙阻力共同控制。"],"optionsEn":["Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth","An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely","Mean open-channel velocity depends on geometry, wetted perimeter, slope and roughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開放渠道的平均流速受斷面形狀、濕周、坡度及粗糙阻力共同控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mean open-channel velocity depends on geometry, wetted perimeter, slope and roughness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b219-v15-30","title":"灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Manning scale for an irrigation canal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Manning scale for an irrigation canal” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s。適用邊界：國際單位制曼寧式、棱柱矩形渠均勻流，糙率為假想值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s. Applicable boundary: SI Manning relation for uniform flow in a prismatic rectangular canal, with assumed roughness. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由實測斷面計算面積與濕周，確認側壁也納入濕周；以沿程水面高程檢查是否近似均勻流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calculate area and wetted perimeter from a surveyed section including both sidewalls, and inspect longitudinal water levels for near-uniform flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s。適用邊界：國際單位制曼寧式、棱柱矩形渠均勻流，糙率為假想值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s. Applicable boundary: SI Manning relation for uniform flow in a prismatic rectangular canal, with assumed roughness.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Manning scale for an irrigation canal\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s。","上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源","總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: b=5 m.","Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources","Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b219-v15-31","title":"灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Manning scale for an irrigation canal: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Manning scale for an irrigation canal” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由實測斷面計算面積與濕周，確認側壁也納入濕周；以沿程水面高程檢查是否近似均勻流。比較量得流量與不同糙率結果，保留植物、沉積與維護狀態，不把糙率當永久固定常數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calculate area and wetted perimeter from a surveyed section including both sidewalls, and inspect longitudinal water levels for near-uniform flow. Compare measured discharge across plausible roughness values while documenting vegetation, deposits and maintenance rather than treating roughness as permanently fixed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把渠道糙率增至零點零三，保持幾何與坡度重算流量，再比較擴寬一公尺的結果，說明兩種改善或劣化不能只用斷面面積判斷。","observationEn":"Site practice: Raise roughness to zero point zero three at fixed geometry and slope, then compare with widening the canal by one metre. Explain why area alone cannot characterize either change in conveyance.","failure":"注意干擾：直接把水深當水力半徑會高估窄渠通量；若下游閘門回水卻仍採底坡為能量坡，則可能得到不符合現地水面線的流量，連帶錯估供水能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Replacing hydraulic radius with depth overstates narrow-channel flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由實測斷面計算面積與濕周，確認側壁也納入濕周；以沿程水面高程檢查是否近似均勻流。比較量得流量與不同糙率結果，保留植物、沉積與維護狀態，不把糙率當永久固定常數。","textEn":"Calculate area and wetted perimeter from a surveyed section including both sidewalls, and inspect longitudinal water levels for near-uniform flow. Compare measured discharge across plausible roughness values while documenting vegetation, deposits and maintenance rather than treating roughness as permanently fixed.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把渠道糙率增至零點零三，保持幾何與坡度重算流量，再比較擴寬一公尺的結果，說明兩種改善或劣化不能只用斷面面積判斷。","textEn":"Raise roughness to zero point zero three at fixed geometry and slope, then compare with widening the canal by one metre. Explain why area alone cannot characterize either change in conveyance.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Manning scale for an irrigation canal\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","由實測斷面計算面積與濕周，確認側壁也納入濕周；以沿程水面高程檢查是否近似均勻流。","每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Calculate area and wetted perimeter from a surveyed section including both sidewalls, and inspect longitudinal water levels for near-uniform flow.","Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"由實測斷面計算面積與濕周，確認側壁也納入濕周；以沿程水面高程檢查是否近似均勻流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calculate area and wetted perimeter from a surveyed section including both sidewalls, and inspect longitudinal water levels for near-uniform flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b219-v15-32","title":"灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Manning scale for an irrigation canal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Manning scale for an irrigation canal” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"直接把水深當水力半徑會高估窄渠通量；若下游閘門回水卻仍採底坡為能量坡，則可能得到不符合現地水面線的流量，連帶錯估供水能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Replacing hydraulic radius with depth overstates narrow-channel flow. Using bed slope as energy slope under downstream backwater can produce a discharge inconsistent with the observed water surface and misstate delivery capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：曼寧式可估算均勻流通水量，但回水、閘門控制或急變流會破壞水面坡與底坡近似相同的條件，需要另作水面線分析。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Manning's relation estimates uniform-flow capacity, while backwater, gates or rapidly varied flow can invalidate the approximation that energy slope follows bed slope and require a water-surface-profile calculation instead.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"直接把水深當水力半徑會高估窄渠通量；若下游閘門回水卻仍採底坡為能量坡，則可能得到不符合現地水面線的流量，連帶錯估供水能力。","textEn":"Replacing hydraulic radius with depth overstates narrow-channel flow. Using bed slope as energy slope under downstream backwater can produce a discharge inconsistent with the observed water surface and misstate delivery capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Manning scale for an irrigation canal\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推","直接把水深當水力半徑會高估窄渠通量；若下游閘門回水卻仍採底坡為能量坡，則可能得到不符合現地水面線的流量，連帶錯估供水能力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely","Replacing hydraulic radius with depth overstates narrow-channel flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"直接把水深當水力半徑會高估窄渠通量；若下游閘門回水卻仍採底坡為能量坡，則可能得到不符合現地水面線的流量，連帶錯估供水能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Replacing hydraulic radius with depth overstates narrow-channel flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b219-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」與「田間淨需水與毛取水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Interpreting crest settlement rate\" and \"Net field need and gross withdrawal\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b219-v15-33","title":"壩頂沉陷的速率解讀：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Interpreting crest settlement rate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Interpreting crest settlement rate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"土石壩壩頂高程隨施工後壓密、材料蠕變、水位及量測基準而改變，兩次高程差除時間只給平均沉陷速率。這個速率不代表未來必然維持直線，也不能單靠向下或向上判斷原因。比較不同測點的空間形狀和時間曲線，通常比單一點的總沉陷量更能辨識差異變形與儀器問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Crest elevation can change through consolidation, creep, reservoir cycles and reference movement. Dividing the difference between two surveys by elapsed time gives only an average settlement rate, not a guaranteed future linear trend or a diagnosis from movement direction alone. Spatial patterns across several points and the shape of the time history are often more informative than one accumulated displacement for distinguishing differential deformation from measurement problems. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Interpreting crest settlement rate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Interpreting crest settlement rate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-33-k1","title":"壩頂沉陷的速率解讀","titleEn":"Interpreting crest settlement rate","text":"土石壩壩頂高程隨施工後壓密、材料蠕變、水位及量測基準而改變，兩次高程差除時間只給平均沉陷速率。這個速率不代表未來必然維持直線，也不能單靠向下或向上判斷原因。","textEn":"Crest elevation can change through consolidation, creep, reservoir cycles and reference movement. Dividing the difference between two surveys by elapsed time gives only an average settlement rate, not a guaranteed future linear trend or a diagnosis from movement direction alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Interpreting crest settlement rate\" is correct?","options":["土石壩壩頂高程隨施工後壓密、材料蠕變、水位及量測基準而改變，兩次高程差除時間只給平均沉陷速率。","兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推","毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率"],"optionsEn":["Crest elevation can change through consolidation, creep, reservoir cycles and reference movement.","An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely","Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency"],"answer":0,"explanation":"土石壩壩頂高程隨施工後壓密、材料蠕變、水位及量測基準而改變，兩次高程差除時間只給平均沉陷速率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Crest elevation can change through consolidation, creep, reservoir cycles and reference movement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b219-v15-34","title":"壩頂沉陷的速率解讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Interpreting crest settlement rate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Interpreting crest settlement rate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day。適用邊界：沉陷向下為正、兩次測量共用穩定基準，僅時段平均速率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day. Applicable boundary: Downward settlement is positive and both surveys share a stable datum; interval-average rate only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以閉合水準測量核對基準穩定，將同日庫水位、氣溫與儀器變更標在沉陷圖上。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Close the leveling survey against stable references and annotate reservoir level, temperature and instrument changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day。適用邊界：沉陷向下為正、兩次測量共用穩定基準，僅時段平均速率。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day. Applicable boundary: Downward settlement is positive and both surveys share a stable datum; interval-average rate only.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Interpreting crest settlement rate\", which statement holds?","options":["孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力","原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day。","不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式"],"optionsEn":["Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton","Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day.","The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b219-v15-35","title":"壩頂沉陷的速率解讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Interpreting crest settlement rate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Interpreting crest settlement rate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以閉合水準測量核對基準穩定，將同日庫水位、氣溫與儀器變更標在沉陷圖上。比較多個壩頂點的差異沉陷，並用至少三個時段查看速率是否加快，避免兩點直線掩蓋曲線轉折。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Close the leveling survey against stable references and annotate reservoir level, temperature and instrument changes. Compare differential settlement across crest points and examine at least three intervals for acceleration, rather than letting a two-point straight line conceal curvature in the trend. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：增加第三次測量，假設再過一百八十日只增加三毫米，計算兩段速率並畫累積曲線，說明平均值相同或不同時仍需查看空間差異。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add a third survey after another one hundred eighty days with only three millimetres of additional settlement. Compare interval rates and cumulative curves, explaining why spatial differences still matter alongside averaged trends.","failure":"注意干擾：用兩次量測直接外推多年會忽略蠕變速率改變；基準點下沉可能讓壩頂看似上升，若未檢查閉合誤差與外部參考，便可能把量測網變動誤判為壩體回彈。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extrapolating years from two observations ignores changing creep rate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以閉合水準測量核對基準穩定，將同日庫水位、氣溫與儀器變更標在沉陷圖上。比較多個壩頂點的差異沉陷，並用至少三個時段查看速率是否加快，避免兩點直線掩蓋曲線轉折。","textEn":"Close the leveling survey against stable references and annotate reservoir level, temperature and instrument changes. Compare differential settlement across crest points and examine at least three intervals for acceleration, rather than letting a two-point straight line conceal curvature in the trend.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"增加第三次測量，假設再過一百八十日只增加三毫米，計算兩段速率並畫累積曲線，說明平均值相同或不同時仍需查看空間差異。","textEn":"Add a third survey after another one hundred eighty days with only three millimetres of additional settlement. Compare interval rates and cumulative curves, explaining why spatial differences still matter alongside averaged trends.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Interpreting crest settlement rate\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多","以閉合水準測量核對基準穩定，將同日庫水位、氣溫與儀器變更標在沉陷圖上。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval","Close the leveling survey against stable references and annotate reservoir level, temperature and instrument changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以閉合水準測量核對基準穩定，將同日庫水位、氣溫與儀器變更標在沉陷圖上。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Close the leveling survey against stable references and annotate reservoir level, temperature and instrument changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b219-v15-36","title":"壩頂沉陷的速率解讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Interpreting crest settlement rate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Interpreting crest settlement rate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用兩次量測直接外推多年會忽略蠕變速率改變；基準點下沉可能讓壩頂看似上升，若未檢查閉合誤差與外部參考，便可能把量測網變動誤判為壩體回彈。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extrapolating years from two observations ignores changing creep rate. A settling reference can make the crest appear to rise, so absent network closure and external checks, reference motion may be mistaken for structural rebound. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較不同測點的空間形狀和時間曲線，通常比單一點的總沉陷量更能辨識差異變形與儀器問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Spatial patterns across several points and the shape of the time history are often more informative than one accumulated displacement for distinguishing differential deformation from measurement problems.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用兩次量測直接外推多年會忽略蠕變速率改變；基準點下沉可能讓壩頂看似上升，若未檢查閉合誤差與外部參考，便可能把量測網變動誤判為壩體回彈。","textEn":"Extrapolating years from two observations ignores changing creep rate. A settling reference can make the crest appear to rise, so absent network closure and external checks, reference motion may be mistaken for structural rebound.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Interpreting crest settlement rate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用兩次量測直接外推多年會忽略蠕變速率改變；基準點下沉可能讓壩頂看似上升，若未檢查閉合誤差與外部參考，便可能把量測網變動誤判為壩體回彈。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率"],"optionsEn":["Extrapolating years from two observations ignores changing creep rate.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency"],"answer":0,"explanation":"用兩次量測直接外推多年會忽略蠕變速率改變；基準點下沉可能讓壩頂看似上升，若未檢查閉合誤差與外部參考，便可能把量測網變動誤判為壩體回彈。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extrapolating years from two observations ignores changing creep rate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b219-v15-37","title":"田間淨需水與毛取水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Net field need and gross withdrawal: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「田間淨需水與毛取水」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Net field need and gross withdrawal” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"灌溉淨需水深度乘田區面積得到作物端水量，除以整體輸配效率才得到水源端毛需求。效率是同一邊界下有用水與取水的比值，若已涵蓋渠道損失，就不能再扣一次。不同作物、降雨及回歸水會改變真正需求，這個固定深度例子只用來練習單位與邊界，不代表實際配水規則。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「田間淨需水與毛取水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Net irrigation depth times field area gives water needed at the crop boundary, while division by delivery efficiency gives gross source withdrawal. Efficiency must refer to consistent boundaries; canal losses included in it cannot be deducted again. Crop choice, rainfall and return flows alter real demand, so this fixed-depth exercise teaches units and accounting rather than prescribing allocation or representing a measured seasonal irrigation requirement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Net field need and gross withdrawal” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「田間淨需水與毛取水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Net field need and gross withdrawal”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-37-k1","title":"田間淨需水與毛取水","titleEn":"Net field need and gross withdrawal","text":"灌溉淨需水深度乘田區面積得到作物端水量，除以整體輸配效率才得到水源端毛需求。效率是同一邊界下有用水與取水的比值，若已涵蓋渠道損失，就不能再扣一次。","textEn":"Net irrigation depth times field area gives water needed at the crop boundary, while division by delivery efficiency gives gross source withdrawal. Efficiency must refer to consistent boundaries; canal losses included in it cannot be deducted again.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「田間淨需水與毛取水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Net field need and gross withdrawal\" is correct?","options":["毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率","灌溉淨需水深度乘田區面積得到作物端水量，除以整體輸配效率才得到水源端毛需求。","上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源"],"optionsEn":["Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency","Net irrigation depth times field area gives water needed at the crop boundary, while division by delivery efficiency gives gross source withdrawal.","Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources"],"answer":1,"explanation":"灌溉淨需水深度乘田區面積得到作物端水量，除以整體輸配效率才得到水源端毛需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Net irrigation depth times field area gives water needed at the crop boundary, while division by delivery efficiency gives gross source withdrawal. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b219-v15-38","title":"田間淨需水與毛取水：定量估算","titleEn":"Net field need and gross withdrawal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「田間淨需水與毛取水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Net field need and gross withdrawal” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3。適用邊界：淨深度已扣有效降雨，效率含假想輸配損失，不再重複扣減。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3. Applicable boundary: Net depth already excludes effective rainfall and efficiency includes assumed conveyance losses, with no second deduction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先將公頃換成平方公尺、毫米換成公尺，再分別列淨需水與毛取水，核對效率分子分母。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert hectares to square metres and millimetres to metres, then list net need and gross withdrawal separately with explicit efficiency boundaries.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3。適用邊界：淨深度已扣有效降雨，效率含假想輸配損失，不再重複扣減。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3. Applicable boundary: Net depth already excludes effective rainfall and efficiency includes assumed conveyance losses, with no second deduction.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「田間淨需水與毛取水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Net field need and gross withdrawal\", which statement holds?","options":["總排水量不變就能證明排水層各處都沒有堵塞","每平方公尺耗散功率就是同數值的局部壓力","原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3。"],"optionsEn":["Unchanged total drainage proves that no part of the drain is blocked","Dissipated power per area is the same numerical local pressure","Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b219-v15-39","title":"田間淨需水與毛取水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Net field need and gross withdrawal: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「田間淨需水與毛取水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Net field need and gross withdrawal” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先將公頃換成平方公尺、毫米換成公尺，再分別列淨需水與毛取水，核對效率分子分母。以渠道入流及田間供水比較估計效率時，要對齊時段並考慮暫存，不能把回歸水直接當完全損失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert hectares to square metres and millimetres to metres, then list net need and gross withdrawal separately with explicit efficiency boundaries. When comparing canal input and field delivery, align periods and account for storage rather than treating all return flow as irrecoverable loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把效率提高到零點八五，計算毛取水減少量與比例，再指出是否能把所有減少量都當流域新水資源，並討論原本回歸水可能已有下游用途。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase efficiency to zero point eight five and calculate gross-withdrawal reduction. Explain why all of that reduction may not become new basin supply when previous return flows already supported downstream uses.","failure":"注意干擾：以淨需水乘效率會把水源需求算得比田間需求還小；若先除效率又再加同一渠道損失，則重複放大需求，導致不同方案比較只是帳目定義不同而非真正節水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying net need by efficiency makes source demand smaller than field need. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先將公頃換成平方公尺、毫米換成公尺，再分別列淨需水與毛取水，核對效率分子分母。以渠道入流及田間供水比較估計效率時，要對齊時段並考慮暫存，不能把回歸水直接當完全損失。","textEn":"Convert hectares to square metres and millimetres to metres, then list net need and gross withdrawal separately with explicit efficiency boundaries. When comparing canal input and field delivery, align periods and account for storage rather than treating all return flow as irrecoverable loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把效率提高到零點八五，計算毛取水減少量與比例，再指出是否能把所有減少量都當流域新水資源，並討論原本回歸水可能已有下游用途。","textEn":"Increase efficiency to zero point eight five and calculate gross-withdrawal reduction. Explain why all of that reduction may not become new basin supply when previous return flows already supported downstream uses.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「田間淨需水與毛取水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Net field need and gross withdrawal\"?","options":["先將公頃換成平方公尺、毫米換成公尺，再分別列淨需水與毛取水，核對效率分子分母。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","發電效率八成就表示兩成水量已被機組消耗"],"optionsEn":["Convert hectares to square metres and millimetres to metres, then list net need and gross withdrawal separately with explicit efficiency boundaries.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Eighty percent generation efficiency means the unit consumes twenty percent of the water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先將公頃換成平方公尺、毫米換成公尺，再分別列淨需水與毛取水，核對效率分子分母。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert hectares to square metres and millimetres to metres, then list net need and gross withdrawal separately with explicit efficiency boundaries. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b219-v15-40","title":"田間淨需水與毛取水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Net field need and gross withdrawal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"prerequisiteIds":["b219-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「田間淨需水與毛取水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Net field need and gross withdrawal” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以淨需水乘效率會把水源需求算得比田間需求還小；若先除效率又再加同一渠道損失，則重複放大需求，導致不同方案比較只是帳目定義不同而非真正節水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying net need by efficiency makes source demand smaller than field need. Dividing by efficiency and then adding the same canal loss inflates demand twice, making apparent savings depend on inconsistent accounting rather than physical improvement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：不同作物、降雨及回歸水會改變真正需求，這個固定深度例子只用來練習單位與邊界，不代表實際配水規則。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Crop choice, rainfall and return flows alter real demand, so this fixed-depth exercise teaches units and accounting rather than prescribing allocation or representing a measured seasonal irrigation requirement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b219-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以淨需水乘效率會把水源需求算得比田間需求還小；若先除效率又再加同一渠道損失，則重複放大需求，導致不同方案比較只是帳目定義不同而非真正節水。","textEn":"Multiplying net need by efficiency makes source demand smaller than field need. Dividing by efficiency and then adding the same canal loss inflates demand twice, making apparent savings depend on inconsistent accounting rather than physical improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]},{"id":"b219-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「田間淨需水與毛取水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Net field need and gross withdrawal\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","以淨需水乘效率會把水源需求算得比田間需求還小；若先除效率又再加同一渠道損失，則重複放大需求，導致不同方案比較只是帳目定義不同而非真正節水。","上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Multiplying net need by efficiency makes source demand smaller than field need.","Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以淨需水乘效率會把水源需求算得比田間需求還小；若先除效率又再加同一渠道損失，則重複放大需求，導致不同方案比較只是帳目定義不同而非真正節水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying net need by efficiency makes source demand smaller than field need. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-tsengwen-owner","v15s-tsengwen-history","b-src-water"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
